  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to compute the average outcome (unweighted) and then count how many outcomes exceed that average. In Lottery B, one outcome (3000) exceeds the average of 0; in Lottery A, 1500 does not exceed its own average (1500). Thus, Lottery B has one outcome above average, while Lottery A has zero. The reason would prefer Lottery B. However, the verbal report does not mention average outcomes, nor does it refer to counting outcomes above the average. Instead, the individual justifies the choice by rejecting risk due to a psychological reframing of loss. There is no evidence that the individual applied or considered the rule of the decision reason. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

